**Extract:**

Fig. 7.1 shows red light travelling from air into a prism made of diamond. The path of the red light is incomplete. The refractive index of diamond is 2.42. At the first boundary of air to diamond, the light ray approaches at an angle of 40 degrees to the normal, and leaves the boundary at an angle x to the normal. At the second boundary, diamond to air, the light ray approaches at angle y to the normal.

Explain the term total internal reflection:
- When light travels from an (optically) more dense medium to an (optically) less dense medium; 
- And the angle of incidence (of the light at the boundary) is greater than the critical angle (of the material creating the boundary); 
- Then all light is reflected OR no light is refracted;

The angle y is greater than the critical angle of diamond.

On Fig. 7.1, draw the path of the red light through and out of the prism after point A.
